From: Waltteri Hooli <wahooli@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] local: drm/msm/a6xx: vote the lowest OPP before the GMU slumbers

With GMU bandwidth voting (info->bcms; x1e80100's X1-85 included) the GPU's GX
corner and DDR bandwidth are voted by the GMU firmware from the GX_BW_PERF_VOTE
it was last given, straight to RPMh, invisible to the Linux interconnect
framework. Measured -- the GMU vote has no readback -- that vote survives
slumber: the prepare-slumber HFI carries bw=0/freq=0 under a TODO and lowers
nothing, and the dev_pm_opp_set_opp(dev, NULL) in a6xx_gmu_stop() drops only
the interconnect vote, which this path does not use. So the DCVS level the GPU
is at when the GMU goes down is what RPMh aggregates for as long as it stays
down.

The devfreq idle clamp (msm_devfreq_idle_work() voting the lowest OPP before
the 66 ms autosuspend fires) would hide this, but a6xx_gpu_init() enables
gpu_clamp_to_idle only on a618 and 7c3 "where this is known not to cause power
supply issues". On every other GMU part each runtime suspend slumbers from the
working level -- on a live desktop that is 687 MHz several times a second -- and
system suspend does the same, from whatever level the compositor had.

On the Lenovo Yoga Slim 7x (X1E-78-100, X1-85) s2idle never reaches the RPMh
sleep set, so the standing ACTIVE votes set the DDR frequency for the whole
suspend (same shape as 0231 for icc-bwmon). The GPU's was the largest, and it
was in the "idle" floor too, because the last runtime suspend before the lid
closed had left the working-level vote behind:

  idle desktop at lid close                 -> s2idle  590 mW   before
  browser video playing at lid close        ->        1324 mW   (lab, 15 min)
  same, real use, 4 h 54 min                ->        1972 mW   (9.7 of 57 Wh)
  video still playing on another workspace  ->        1406 mW
  idle desktop at lid close, this patch     ->         152 mW   (15 min, 11 % charge)

Vote the lowest OPP through the GMU in a6xx_gmu_shutdown(), after the GMU is
confirmed idle and before the bus halt and the slumber request. This is the
clamp, applied at the one point every slumber passes through, without changing
the frequency the GPU runs at while awake. The hung path still goes to
force_off untouched, and a6xx_gmu_set_freq() is a no-op when the GMU already
sits at the floor. A dev_dbg records the level it came from; it fires on most
runtime suspends of a live desktop, so it is dynamic-debug only:

  echo 'file a6xx_gmu.c +p' > /sys/kernel/debug/dynamic_debug/control
  slumber from 687 MHz: voting 300 MHz first

Resume is unaffected: a6xx_gmu_set_initial_freq() brings the GPU up at the
level recorded here and devfreq re-evaluates from the GMU's own frequency
(a6xx_gmu_get_freq) on its next sample.
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
@@ -1203,6 +1203,33 @@
 	dev_pm_opp_put(gpu_opp);
 }
 
+/*
+ * The GMU keeps its last GX_BW_PERF_VOTE across slumber: prepare-slumber carries
+ * no fallback level, and the dev_pm_opp_set_opp(NULL) in a6xx_gmu_stop() only
+ * drops the Linux interconnect vote, which GMU bandwidth voting does not use. So
+ * the DDR bandwidth the GPU was at when it went down stays voted at RPMh until
+ * the GMU comes back -- through every runtime suspend, since the devfreq idle
+ * clamp is only enabled on a618/7c3, and through system suspend. Slumber from
+ * the floor instead. On x1e80100 this is ~440 mW of s2idle.
+ */
+static void a6xx_gmu_set_lowest_freq(struct msm_gpu *gpu, struct a6xx_gmu *gmu)
+{
+	struct dev_pm_opp *gpu_opp;
+	unsigned long freq = 0;
+
+	gpu_opp = dev_pm_opp_find_freq_ceil(&gpu->pdev->dev, &freq);
+	if (IS_ERR(gpu_opp))
+		return;
+
+	/* Fires on most runtime suspends of a live desktop; dynamic debug only. */
+	if (freq != gmu->freq)
+		dev_dbg(gmu->dev, "slumber from %lu MHz: voting %lu MHz first\n",
+			gmu->freq / 1000000, freq / 1000000);
+
+	a6xx_gmu_set_freq(gpu, gpu_opp, false);
+	dev_pm_opp_put(gpu_opp);
+}
+
 static void a6xx_gmu_set_initial_bw(struct msm_gpu *gpu, struct a6xx_gmu *gmu)
 {
 	struct dev_pm_opp *gpu_opp;
@@ -1510,6 +1537,8 @@
 	if (ret)
 		goto force_off;
 
+	a6xx_gmu_set_lowest_freq(&adreno_gpu->base, gmu);
+
 	adreno_gpu->funcs->bus_halt(adreno_gpu, a6xx_gpu->hung);
 
 	/* tell the GMU we want to slumber */
